# API resource enrichment wiring

**Service returns data ≠ UI receives data.** A common failure: batch-compute enrichment in the controller, stash it on `$request->attributes`, read it inside `JsonResource::toArray()` — the service/tinker path passes while **HTTP JSON is always `null`**.

Real example (fixed): `ModelKitSeriesResolutionService::resolveBatch()` worked; `series_resolution` in taxonomy verifications API was always `null` because paginated `Resource::collection()` did not reliably pass request attributes to each resource row.

## Forbidden patterns

| Pattern | Why it fails |
| --- | --- |
| `$request->attributes->set('foo_by_id', …)` then read in `JsonResource` | Request bag is not a reliable per-row side channel for paginated collections |
| "Service/tinker returns X" as sole proof | Bypasses controller → resource → JSON path the SPA actually calls |
| UI handoff when dialog reads `item.computed_field` but API field never spot-checked | Operator sees empty/fallback UI despite "wired" backend |

```php
// ❌ BAD — enrichment may never appear in JSON
$request->attributes->set('series_resolutions_by_sku', $this->series->resolveBatch($products));
return ProductTaxonomyVerificationResource::collection($paginator);
```

## Required patterns (pick one)

**1. Runtime property on the row model/DTO (preferred for list endpoints)**

Attach enrichment on each item **before** wrapping in a Resource:

```php
$resolutionsBySku = $this->series->resolveBatch($products);

foreach ($paginator->getCollection() as $verification) {
    $verification->loadedSeriesResolution = $resolutionsBySku[(string) $verification->product->sku] ?? null;
}

return ProductTaxonomyVerificationResource::collection($paginator);
```

Resource reads `$this->resource->loadedSeriesResolution` — document runtime-only properties on the model with `@property` / a public typed field.

**2. Explicit resource construction** — `new MyResource($row, $enrichment)` when the collection is small or non-paginated.

**3. Merge into the service result** — for single-object endpoints, return a DTO/array that already includes computed keys; Resource maps 1:1.

Do **not** reintroduce request-bag side channels to avoid touching the model.

## Cross-layer verification (mandatory for new computed API fields)

When the SPA reads a **new or changed** JSON field (dialog, row badge, tooltip):

1. **Service** — prove on realistic fixture (tinker/Pest/service test).
2. **HTTP** — hit the **same route** the SPA uses; assert the JSON path is present and non-null when the service would populate it (`Invoke-RestMethod`, Pest `getJson`, or Playwright intercept — not tinker alone).
3. **UI** — open the surface that consumes the field; empty fallback copy when data exists = **not done**.

Intent contract line:

> When [list/detail API for route X] → response row includes `[field]` with expected shape when [service preconditions hold].

## Regression minimum (bug-fix or new enrichment)

When fixing or adding computed list fields:

- **Pest feature test** on the HTTP route asserting JSON path, **or**
- **E2e** asserting the UI is not showing the empty/fallback state for a row that should have data.

Test must fail on the request-bag wiring anti-pattern.

## Checklist before handoff

- [ ] Enrichment attached on the **row** (or explicit Resource arg), not on `$request->attributes`
- [ ] `JsonResource` reads from `$this->resource`, not `$request->attributes->get(...)` for per-item data
- [ ] HTTP response spot-checked on real route + sample row
- [ ] UI/dialog checked when user-visible

